From 8378e042d066a2f1619b271b96c63e0ee058f69c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pasta <pasta@dashboost.org>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 06:59:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] test: record the vectors embedded in the C++ unit tests
 as JSON

Add test/util/o4_dump.h and call it from the tests that hold hand-embedded vectors
(pow, subsidy, SML entries, ISDLOCK, DIP14, quorum proof, dynamic thresholds, block reward
reallocation, DIP0020 opcodes, CHECKDATASIG). With O4_VECTOR_OUT set to a directory, each
test also writes what Core computed next to the check it already makes, as <name>.json.
Without it the recording code does not run, and no existing assertion is changed.

With recording on, checkdatasig_tests additionally fails if two flag sets that are equal
under the mask it records produce different outcomes, which is what lets 4096 random flag
sets collapse into a handful of records.

Node program task O4 (rust-dashcore test-vectors/). Local branch only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
